  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on stated preference survey data rather than observed travel behavior in an active, real-world UAM market.",
      "what": "This study analyzed user preferences and price sensitivity for shared versus solo Urban Air Mobility (UAM) services using a stated preference survey. The researchers developed a hybrid choice model that integrates demographic interactions, environmental awareness, and price sensitivity to evaluate trade-offs between travel time, cost, waiting time, and passenger capacity.",
      "why": "It establishes that environmental awareness and demographic-specific price sensitivity are key mediating factors in UAM adoption, demonstrating that shared flight models can lower per-passenger costs through higher vehicle utilization while appealing to environmentally conscious travelers."
